# RDF-star 1.1 constellation dataset — the wire twin of RDF12_ROWS.
#
# Authored in RDF-star **1.1** `<< s p o >>` syntax on purpose: RDF 1.2
# ships the triple-term form `<<( s p o )>>` and the reifier bnode
# (`_:b rdf:reifies <<( s p o )>>`), and Fuseki / GraphDB 10.x currently
# REJECT the 1.2 form on ingest (HTTP 400). The 1.1 quoted-triple form
# ingests today and is round-trip compatible with pyoxigraph 0.3+, so
# this file loads into any RDF-star store while carrying the same
# annotation shape the two projections consume.
#
# Verified 2026-08-14 with pyoxigraph 0.5.9:
#   $ python3 -c "import pyoxigraph as p; \
#       print(len(list(p.parse(path='constellation.trig', format=p.RdfFormat.TRIG))))"
#   17
# (pyoxigraph 0.5 auto-migrates classic `<< s p o >>` to the RDF 1.2
#  reifier-bnode form `_:b rdf:reifies <<( s p o )>>`, so the on-disk
#  1.1 form parses as 1.2 triple-terms with a synthetic reifier per
#  annotated fact — round-trippable in either direction.)

@prefix sat:  <http://example.org/sat#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

# -- Base facts as quoted triples, each annotated ----------------------

<< sat:aquila1 sat:hasMass "950"^^xsd:decimal >>
    sat:statedBy    sat:engineering ;
    sat:confidence  "0.9"^^xsd:decimal ;
    sat:recordedAt  "2026-02-01"^^xsd:date .

<< sat:aquila1 sat:orbits sat:earth >>
    sat:statedBy    sat:flightDynamics ;
    sat:confidence  "1.0"^^xsd:decimal .

<< sat:commsBus sat:band sat:kaBand >>
    sat:statedBy    sat:rfTeam ;
    sat:confidence  "0.8"^^xsd:decimal .

<< sat:aquila1 sat:relaysTo sat:groundOps >>
    sat:statedBy    sat:missionOps ;
    sat:confidence  "0.7"^^xsd:decimal .

# -- Nested: a statement ABOUT another statement ----------------------
# QA reviewed the mass fact's confidence assertion — the outer quoted
# triple has a QUOTED TRIPLE as its subject. This is the shape the
# haunt-style edge render cannot express without a synthetic anchor,
# and the hyperarc render handles as a statement-to-statement link.

<< << sat:aquila1 sat:hasMass "950"^^xsd:decimal >>
     sat:confidence
     "0.9"^^xsd:decimal >>
   sat:reviewedBy sat:qa ;
   sat:statedBy   sat:qa .

# -- Forward-form (RDF 1.2 triple-term) equivalent, kept as reference
#    text so the file remains parseable today. Uncomment when your
#    downstream store advertises RDF-1.2 acceptance.
#
# _:b1 rdf:reifies <<( sat:aquila1 sat:hasMass "950"^^xsd:decimal )>> ;
#      sat:statedBy sat:engineering ;
#      sat:confidence "0.9"^^xsd:decimal .
